# Navigation across interactive surfaces (2026-11-16)
#
# One of four readings of the babble seed, through one lens: how fluently a hand moves across factshift.center and spw.quest.
# Read from source and from the workbench's own tools. Nothing was driven in a browser and nothing was heard. Everything here is an open wonder for the owner to judge.

#>babble_navigation_2026_11_16
#:journal #!babble
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"found"{
 pins: "The seed's pins line went stale while this was read. The canvas branch edge-submenus gained 423f520 and d4e3979, and the canvas's main was fast-forwarded from 1a4157a to d4e3979 at 10:25 local on 2026-11-16. Every canvas citation here is at 1a4157a, the commit the seed calls deployed, unless it names d4e3979. Only edge-scrub.ts, frame-refresh.ts, tool-steps.ts and two stylesheets differ between the two."
 still_holds: "Three findings below are already answered at d4e3979: the swallowed click (said_not_done), two gestures on one touch (facet gestures, one_touch_two), and the rail of three scales (rail_three_scales). The rest sit in files that did not change between the two commits and hold at both: pinch's meanings and the spread that ends in a page load, the fold word that does not match the fold, the two seatings of the walls, the inverse nothing reads, and, in the workbench, the seam spw hear cannot sound."
 prefixes: "c: is the site consumer's workers/factshift-center/app/src. q: is the site consumer's workers/spw-quest/src. s: is the site consumer's .spw. w: is the workbench at cf41ca22."
 grammar_exists: "The canvas already states a gesture grammar, keyed by what the hand does and not by kind of change: tap acts, hold grips, a sideways swipe chooses, an up or down swipe reaches for more or less, hold then drag places (c:js/ui/gestures.ts:1-8). Tempo is a second axis: slow changes an amount, quick changes a state (c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:1, :38). Pinch is in neither list."
 pinch_many: "Two fingers closing or spreading make four of the audit's six kinds of change across factshift.center and spw.quest, through eleven meanings chosen by where they land and how fast: the size of a thing, the camera's scale, a page load, a fold, and a primed edit of the line (facet gestures, rows pinch_scale to pinch_edit, and pinch_eleven)."
 said_not_done: "At 1a4157a a right rail stop that presses a control or a swatch says it happened and does nothing: the release opens the scrub's click-swallow window and then clicks into it (c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:783-785, :726-731, :560-580). Read from source. The message of 423f520 reports the same fault driven in a browser and fixed by letting untrusted clicks through (frame-refresh.ts:756 at d4e3979); the message of d4e3979 reports a re-check passing."
 rail_three_scales: "With menus closed the left rail at 1a4157a holds up to 34 stops of three scales on one strip: 10 tree items, 12 bodies, 12 lines (c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:455, :447, :438), 7 shown at a time (:513), 32 px a stop (:385). One 32 px step can load a file, refit the camera to a body, or hold another line."
 cuts_inside: "Zoom and cut sit the wrong way round. Where content changes kind (workspace to document, word to letters) the canvas already cuts. Its hardest cuts, a page load to enter a node and a rebuilt stage to leave the file map, sit inside the range where it draws every depth the same way (facet zoom)."
 wall_seating: "The four walls turn in two different seatings across the surfaces: concept, scene, mode, body in the workbench pivot reader, the canvas joints and the canvas long-press ring; mode, body, scene, concept in spw.quest's tap order and the canvas node ring (facet sides, four_seating)."
 hear_seam: "spw hear cannot tell a list from a sequence: day{wake, eat, sleep} and day{wake; eat; sleep} wrote byte-identical WAV files of two clicks each (facet art_music)."
 inverse_unread: "Nine of the 29 action shapes the canvas infers for its menu name an inverse, and no code reads the field (c:js/ui/interaction-tree.ts:15, :108-178)."
 cue_not_act: "The pinch note on a body arms its fold word at a scale of 0.68 or less at any speed (c:js/ui/scale-cue.ts:53), and the fold happens at 0.8 or less only when the pinch ends inside 280 ms (c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:38, :41, :297-306). A slow pinch to 0.66 is told fold and gets a smaller body; a quick one to 0.75 folds with no word."
}

^"gestures"{
 # The audit, at 1a4157a. One row is one gesture making one kind of change, with where. Kinds: scale, sequence (or time), turn, edit (the line or the graph is rewritten), selection, view (the camera, a fold, a page, a tool: a change of view or of kind).
 tap_selection: "A tap on a node with no tool in hand toggles its selection (c:js/simulation/nodes/handling/circle.ts:337); a tap on empty ground clears it (c:js/simulation/events.ts:162)."
 tap_view: "A second tap on the one selected node that can be a page loads its page (circle.ts:334); a tap on a region frames it with the camera and a second tap comes back (c:js/modes/spw/file-map.ts:237-238); a tap on a body's title folds it (file-map.ts:229); a tap on a mapped line replaces the map with that line (file-map.ts:250-252)."
 tap_edit: "Two taps on a node inside 320 ms open its name to rewrite (circle.ts:188, :319)."
 tap_turn: "A tap on a primed joint makes its turn, a wall turned or a mark changed (c:js/modes/spw/operator-field.ts:231)."
 hold_scale: "A node held 420 ms opens its ring, and a slide past grow or shrink sizes it by reach (circle.ts:56, :417, :468)."
 hold_edit: "The same ring links, removes, drops a part from the line or renames it (c:js/simulation/nodes/verb-ring.ts:20-31; c:js/simulation/nodes/line-verbs.ts:74, :86); empty ground held 450 ms opens a ring that adds a wall or a node to the held line (events.ts:40-47, :129)."
 hold_turn: "The ring's up-right turns a part's or a scene's braces to the next empty pair (line-verbs.ts:39, :93)."
 hold_sequence: "The ring's left and right move a part earlier or later in its body (line-verbs.ts:88-89)."
 hold_selection: "The ring's up-left selects (verb-ring.ts:30)."
 hold_view: "A joint held 320 ms primes going into that slot as its own page (operator-field.ts:15, :175, :123); a gesture surface held 420 ms only shows its card (c:js/ui/gestures.ts:53, :117-123)."
 drag_view: "A dragged node is placed where it is let go (circle.ts:685); a dragged body moves (c:js/simulation/rects/region-rects.ts:183); a dragged handle carries its tool (c:js/ui/focal-point.ts:364-381)."
 drag_flow: "A node let go fast is thrown and goes home; slow, it stays (circle.ts:653, :683)."
 drag_edit: "A node dropped on a node links or unlinks them (circle.ts:645); dropped inside one of the line's containers it rewrites the line (circle.ts:656, :662)."
 drag_scale: "A body dragged from within 24 px of a side edge moves that side (region-rects.ts:173-181; body-gestures.ts:44)."
 drag_selection: "Alt with a drag on the ground draws a marquee (events.ts:183)."
 flick_sequence: "A quick flick sideways inside a body steps its parts, and in from a body's side edge frames the sibling before or after (body-gestures.ts:225-232)."
 flick_view: "A flick up or down steps the body's stratum (as written, by its parts, as particles), and the two diagonals move the camera out or in a level (body-gestures.ts:233-234, :246-252)."
 flick_selection: "A flick up-left selects the body's parts (body-gestures.ts:235-239)."
 flick_edit: "A flick down-right opens the body as written to rewrite (body-gestures.ts:240-245)."
 swipe_sequence: "A sideways swipe steps the lines this browser held on the hash (c:js/ui/hash-gestures.ts:84-85), the thread or those lines on the corner box (c:js/ui/held-expressions.ts:59-60), a joint's turns (operator-field.ts:209-212), and a tool's levels on the lens (focal-point.ts:390-431)."
 swipe_view: "On the lens, left opens the tool column and down the menu (focal-point.ts:394, :132)."
 swipe_edit: "On the lens, up adds a node where the swipe lets go (focal-point.ts:428); right takes what the tool has primed, as on a tool's tile (focal-point.ts:60; c:js/ui/tool-tiles.ts:13)."
 pinch_scale: "Two fingers resize the node between them, else the selection, else every node (c:js/simulation/pinch.ts:186-190, :340); a slow pinch resizes a body (body-gestures.ts:284-292); on the title it resizes the title (c:js/ui/title-layout.ts:127-134)."
 pinch_view: "A pinch begun on the lens, or on a stage with no nodes, zooms the camera between 0.35 and 3 (pinch.ts:32-33, :344-348, :555); a spread to 1.35 on a node that can be a page loads that page, and a close to 0.65 inside one loads its parent (pinch.ts:42-52, :277-280); a quick pinch folds or opens a body (body-gestures.ts:295-305)."
 pinch_turn: "A spread on a joint primes a turn of that room's walls (operator-field.ts:190-193)."
 pinch_edit: "A pinch on a joint primes dropping the room (operator-field.ts:194-197), and on spw.quest's pivot it primes dropping the slot (q:pivot.js:609)."
 wheel_view: "A two-finger scroll pans the camera (pinch.ts:455-458); with ctrl over the lens it zooms it (pinch.ts:587-593)."
 wheel_scale: "A wheel with ctrl resizes the node under the pointer, else the selection, else every node, or a body (pinch.ts:396-402, :424-441), and past 1.35 or 0.65 loads a page as a pinch does (pinch.ts:427-438)."
 left_scrub_sequence: "Released on a stop, the left rail holds a line of the thread, opens a tool, focuses a menu row, or steps the concept history (c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:621-623, :556-559, :550-552, :644-646)."
 left_scrub_view: "The same rail loads a file of the tree, refits the camera to a body or to a selected node, or reloads the page (frame-refresh.ts:632-634, :624-630, :635-642, :647-649)."
 right_scrub_any: "Released on a verb, the right rail runs it, whatever it does, and with menus closed it runs a recent act again (frame-refresh.ts:553-555, :582-620; c:js/ui/hotkey-buttons.ts:156-185)."
 pull_view: "A pull of 64 px down from the title reloads the page (frame-refresh.ts:76, :740-743, :345)."
 edge_swipe_sequence: "A swipe of 56 px in from a 72 px side band runs the frame's left or right act: the line or body before or after, the held line earlier or later, the concept back or forward, the tool or verb before or after (frame-refresh.ts:77-79, :744-745, :779-786; c:js/ui/frame-context.ts:156-165, :186-187, :258-263, :297-298, :320-321)."
 edge_swipe_selection: "With nodes selected the same swipe steps to the next node, or narrows, grows or inverts the selection (frame-context.ts:209-210, :219-228)."
 keys_sequence: "Up and down step the thread, as do PageUp, PageDown, Home and End; left and right step the concept history (c:js/init/hotkeys/_.ts:213, :219, :223-232, :200, :207)."
 keys_view: "Shift with an arrow walks bodies and refits the camera to each (hotkeys/_.ts:198-218; body-gestures.ts:168); a digit opens a tool (hotkeys/_.ts:101); Shift with a brace folds (hotkeys/_.ts:278); Escape lets go of the field, the menu, the selection, then the tool (hotkeys/_.ts:250)."
 keys_selection: "Ctrl A selects every node and Tab walks them (hotkeys/_.ts:311, :167)."
 keys_edit: "Delete removes the selection (hotkeys/_.ts:330); in the line's field Alt with up or down moves a part (c:js/modes/spw/line-edit.ts:280)."
 keys_flow: "Plus and minus change the charge between every node (hotkeys/_.ts:154, :161)."
 # Every place one gesture makes more than one kind of change.
 many_kinds: "Kinds per gesture, counted from the rows above: tap 4, hold 6, drag 4 and flow, flick 4, swipe 3, pinch 4, wheel 2, left scrub 2, edge swipe 2, keys 4 and flow. The right scrub makes whatever its verb makes. Only the pull down makes one."
 pinch_eleven: "Pinch alone has eleven meanings on the two hosts: the size of a node, of the selection, of every node, of a body, of the title; the camera; entering a page; going up a page; a fold; a primed wall turn; a primed drop. The canvas says which is under the fingers with a plane tag (node, selection, canvas, body, stage; c:js/ui/scale-cue.ts:6, :62-93)."
 one_touch_two: "At 1a4157a one touch at the very edge can run two gestures: the edge scrub takes it at pointerdown and the frame's own swipe also accepts it when it lands on the root element, so a release can commit a stop and also clear the selection, close the tool or reload (frame-refresh.ts:687-724, :862-871, :894-908). 423f520 adds a claimed pointer that the frame declines (frame-refresh.ts:744 at d4e3979)."
 # Every change more than one gesture makes.
 shared_thread: "Eight ways step the thread: up and down, PageUp and PageDown, Home and End (hotkeys/_.ts:213-232), the frame's sideways swipe (frame-context.ts:297-298), the swipe in from an edge (frame-refresh.ts:744-745), the corner box's swipe and its two buttons (held-expressions.ts:59-60, :199, :203), and the left rail (frame-refresh.ts:621-623). Keys put lines on up and down; every swipe puts them on left and right."
 shared_camera: "At least nine move the camera: a lens pinch (pinch.ts:555), a scroll (pinch.ts:456-457), a tap on a region (file-map.ts:238), Shift with an arrow (body-gestures.ts:168), the frame's up or down in a document (frame-refresh.ts:307-312), a body flick (body-gestures.ts:246-252), a left rail body stop (frame-refresh.ts:627), the tree trail (c:js/ui/tree-trail.ts:67-68), and the corner chip's reset (held-expressions.ts:146)."
 shared_node_size: "Four size a node: a pinch (pinch.ts:340), a wheel with ctrl (pinch.ts:441), the ring by reach (circle.ts:468), and the menu's larger and smaller (interaction-tree.ts:127-128)."
 shared_wall_turn: "Five turn a wall: a joint tapped twice or swiped (operator-field.ts:231, :212), a spread on a joint (operator-field.ts:190-193), the ring's up-right (line-verbs.ts:93), a part dragged into another container (circle.ts:656), and on spw.quest a tap or a swipe on a part (q:pivot.js:578-586)."
 shared_fold: "Four fold a body: a quick pinch (body-gestures.ts:303), a tap on its title (file-map.ts:229), Shift with a brace (hotkeys/_.ts:278), a flick down to as written (body-gestures.ts:234)."
 shared_enter: "Four enter a node as a page: a second tap (circle.ts:334), a spread (pinch.ts:277), the frame's up with one node selected (frame-refresh.ts:255-257), a held joint pressed (operator-field.ts:123)."
 shared_reload: "Four reload: the pull down (frame-refresh.ts:345), the corner button (frame-refresh.ts:850), the left rail's refresh stop (frame-refresh.ts:647-649), the frame's down swipe past 64 px with nothing open (frame-refresh.ts:900-907)."
 no_twist: "Nothing on either host reads a twist: the only angles taken are a flick's sector, the ring's verb, and a thrown node's lean (body-gestures.ts:227; verb-ring.ts:49; circle.ts:557)."
 scroll_is_space: "A scroll never steps a sequence on the canvas; it pans, and with ctrl it sizes (pinch.ts:384-464). Sequence lives on swipes, arrows and the rails."
 five_times: "There are at least five sequences a step could mean: the thread, the lines this browser held (16 kept; c:js/ui/document-place.ts:1-6), the concept history (c:js/ui/concept-history.ts:1-9), kept frames (hash-gestures.ts:122), and the last 14 acts (c:js/ui/activation-trail.ts:25). One gesture for sequence would still have to say which."
}

^"zoom"{
 # Every scale the canvas has at 1a4157a and how a hand moves between them. The test used for each move: do the same nodes stay on the stage (a camera move), is the node collection replaced, or does the page load again.
 test: "A zoom earns its continuity only where the same nodes stay on the stage. The source separates three mechanisms cleanly: zoomToBox keeps the nodes and eases the camera for 260 ms (c:js/simulation/pinch.ts:122, :131-161); holding a line and leaving the file map rebuild the line's nodes (c:js/modes/spw/spw-talk.ts:128-133, :245; c:js/modes/spw/held-line.ts:45-48; c:js/modes/spw/file-map.ts:74-80, :250-252); entering a node and going up load the page again (c:js/modes/spw/frame-page.ts:70; c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:316)."
 rebuild_keeps: "The rebuild is not a clean break: loose nodes stay, and a node of the new line with the same role and name as one of the old keeps its place, its size and its pin (c:js/modes/spw/line-anatomy.ts:1171-1212). A word that recurs from line to line already holds still across a cut."
 workspace: "The workspace is a tree of directories and files kept in the browser (c:js/modes/spw/spw-tree.ts:32). It is never drawn on the stage: it is a list in the corner drawer and on the left rail (c:js/ui/held-expressions.ts:91-95; c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:199-208). Workspace to document loads a file's text as a new thread (spw-talk.ts:164, :136). Content changes kind (paths to lines) and the move is already a cut."
 tree_crawler: "The crawler follows a line's path references on demand and adds what it fetches to the tree (spw-tree.ts:533). It is reach, not scale: the list grows; nothing gets nearer."
 document_map: "A file drawn as a map is one dot a line, gathered by operator, lens, frame or shape (file-map.ts:132-211). Map to cluster is a camera move over the same dots (file-map.ts:238): self-similar, and the zoom is earned. Cluster to line replaces the dots with one line's anatomy (file-map.ts:250-252): a dot becomes a figure, content changes kind, and the cut fits."
 document_whole: "A file drawn whole is every line's full anatomy in its own cell, at the nested size past four lines (file-map.ts:83-129, :91). Whole to cell is a camera move (file-map.ts:233-238). Cell to line then rebuilds the stage for content that was already drawn (file-map.ts:250-252): one of the two places a zoom would be earned and a cut is used; node_to_page is the other."
 line_to_body: "Line to body to nested body is a camera move over the same nodes (file-map.ts:238; c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:98, :168). The content is self-similar by construction: a part that is an expression is laid out by the same function one depth down, the same at every depth (c:js/modes/spw/line-anatomy.ts:72, :1004). It has two sizes only, 34 at depth zero and 24 at every depth below (line-anatomy.ts:118-119, :217), so going deeper does not show the same picture smaller again."
 node_to_page: "Entering a node makes its own expression the line of a new page by a page load, and going up is another (frame-page.ts:59-71; frame-refresh.ts:313-319). The content is the most self-similar step there is, an expression inside an expression, and it gets the hardest cut in the app. One of its four gestures is a spread, a continuous motion that ends in a load, with a note that says keep at 1.16 and enter at 1.35 (c:js/ui/scale-cue.ts:33-38; pinch.ts:42-52). The cut has a reason that is not kind: the page is a save boundary (frame-page.ts:8-11)."
 strata: "A body read as written, by its parts, or as particles is three kinds of picture of one body (c:js/modes/spw/brace-folds.ts:1-8), stepped by a flick. A lens swap, done as a step. One of its gestures is still a pinch (body-gestures.ts:295-305)."
 word_to_letters: "Below a word there is no stage: a rename opens a text field over the node and the line is rewritten when the field settles (c:js/simulation/editable-node.ts:152-181). Letters are never nodes, and nothing at this commit reads humps (no match for camel or hump under c:). In the line's own field the nearest thing is a ladder of selection, word to part to room to line (c:js/modes/spw/line-edit.ts:5-6, :267). So the owner's scene of zooming into an identifier lands today on a cut to a text field."
 plane_scale: "The cognitive-plane scale is not a scale to travel. It is five names for what the present pinch is scaling: node, selection, canvas, body, stage (scale-cue.ts:1-6)."
 fractal_summary: "The fractal summary is the one zoom in the source that is a reduction and not a shrinking: the same line said a level shorter, each depth's summary the shape of the whole (c:js/modes/spw/line-summary.ts:1-4, :107, :114). No hand drives it: its only callers pass 34 and 30 characters (held-expressions.ts:180, :293)."
 runtime: "A run drawn as nodes (at most 24 registers and 28 state values; c:js/modes/spw/workbench-runtime.ts:31-33, :1367) replaces what is drawn with another kind of thing: a lens swap."
 other_dials: "Three more things scale without changing what is seen: a node's radius, 6 to 160 (pinch.ts:38-39); the title, 0.5 to 1.6 (c:js/ui/title-layout.ts:18-19); the camera, 0.35 to 3, a range of 8.6 (pinch.ts:32-33)."
 doubt_tested: "The owner's doubt, tried against the source: between workspace and document, and between word and letters, the canvas does not zoom at all. What reads as zoom across kinds is three other things: a rail that ran files, bodies and lines on one strip (facet found, rail_three_scales); a spread that ends in a page load; and a camera that refits on every body step. The doubt holds about the feel and misnames the cause."
 babble_tested: "The babble's reply, tried the same way: document, line, body and part are not different kinds here. They are one recursive kind drawn one way at every depth, and a file drawn whole is that drawing tiled. The kinds that differ are at the two ends, the tree of files above and the letters below, and both ends are already cuts (facet broken, zoom_doubt)."
 refit: "Each body stop refits the camera to that body: k is the stage's width over the body's width plus twice the pad, clamped to 0.35 and 3 (pinch.ts:135). Nested boxes run from 150 to 280 px wide (line-anatomy.ts:154-155), so on a stage 390 px wide two sibling bodies can sit at 1.70 and 1.08 with the rail's pad of 40 (frame-refresh.ts:627), a change of 1.57 in one step. Equal steps of the hand give unequal steps of the view. Computed from constants by width alone; not measured."
}

^"sides"{
 # Left and right, then what already comes in twos and fours, then the frame turned.
 where_how: "Deployed at 1a4157a: the left rail is where, the right is how (c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:1-2, :396-399). The left holds menu rows, tools, the tree with the bodies and the thread, the selection's members, the concept history (edge-scrub.ts:243-320); the right holds a family's verbs, a tool's controls, swatches, and recent acts (edge-scrub.ts:327-388)."
 arms: "The arms reading is the workbench's: marks before a name act before it is read, marks after it on what it yields (w:packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pivots.ts:5-6, :56-59). On two rails the left would hold the pivots of what stands before a name and the right the pivots of what follows it. Tried on the owner's line: of the 11 pivots of =foo@(<bar>), 3 turn foo, 1 turns bar, and 7 turn the bond between them. Most of that line's nuance belongs to neither side."
 arms_probe: `=foo@(<bar>): parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 2; line whole true, bond @ tight; spoken configuration foo, perspective, scene concept bar; pivots 11 (10 read): bond 3, spacing 1, exchange 1, attach 2, side 1, mark 2, walls 1`
 objective_subjective: "Objective and subjective is the site consumer's canon, tied to the opening and the closing brace (s:conventions/asset-management.spw:94-95; s:conventions/operator-semantics.spw:89-90; s:conventions/site-semantics.spw:42-43). Neither word occurs under c:. Read onto the rails, the left would hold what any reader can open by address and the right what belongs to this reader's visit."
 objective_subjective_moves: "Of the 12 kinds of stop a rail can commit (edge-scrub.ts:82-94), three depend on this visit: a recent act, a member of the selection, a step of the concept history. Today the first is on the right and the other two on the left (edge-scrub.ts:380-387, :280-294, :296-318). Objective and subjective is the only reading in play that would move a stop across; it would also leave a tool's verbs, which every reader shares, without an obvious side."
 large_small: "Large and small is the site consumer's third reading (s:caches/motion-and-marks-2026-11.spw:79). At d4e3979 it is what a tool's rails already do: its cards on the left, the controls of the card in hand on the right (c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:304-342 at d4e3979)."
 before_after: "The source has a fourth reading the seed does not name: the left edge is the one before and the right edge the one after. A swipe in from the left goes back and from the right goes forward (c:js/ui/concept-history.ts:8-9; c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:660), and a body's left edge is called the opener's side and frames the sibling before it (c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:13-16, :224-226)."
 potential_action: "And a fifth: left is potential and right is action. The gesture table gives left the mark ~ and right the mark ! (c:js/ui/interaction-tree.ts:44-51); on the lens, left opens the tool column and right takes what the tool has primed (c:js/ui/focal-point.ts:391-419). The site consumer's charge rule says the same of braces: the opening one gathers, the closing one discharges (s:conventions/operator-semantics.spw:163), and the canvas's Escape is commented as mirroring a right brace's discharge (c:js/init/hotkeys/_.ts:249)."
 actors_side: "A sixth is a warning: the stage's nine marks are named from the actor's side, so stage right is on the reader's left (c:ts/simulation/stage-mark.ts:1-4, :20-24). It is the one place in the source where left and right already flip with who is naming them."
 agree: "Where and how, large and small, before and after, potential and action, and the arms reading all point the same way: the left is context, the right is what comes of it. They would fill the rails alike. A choice among them changes words, not stops."
 two_exists: "What already comes in twos: two rails 28 px wide and two swipe bands 72 px wide (frame-refresh.ts:78-79); a joined line drawn as two halves with a gap of 4 percent and its bond between (c:js/modes/spw/line-anatomy.ts:159, :835-843); a body's opener side and closer side, 24 px each (body-gestures.ts:44, :315-319); a brace pair as two particles of opposite charge (line-anatomy.ts:500); handle and lens (focal-point.ts:356-363); prime and actualize (c:js/modes/spw/operator-field.ts:1-7; q:pivot.js:311-313); slow and quick (body-gestures.ts:1); two menus and two orientations (c:js/ui/frame-context.ts:11-12)."
 two_hemispheric: "A hemispheric canvas maps onto the joined line as drawn: gardener@garden is already a left half, a right half and a bond, and the workbench's exchange pivot already swaps them (w:packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pivots.ts:329). It would have to invent the second half of a line that has no bond, and a place for a bond's own pivots, which are seven of the eleven in =foo@(<bar>)."
 joined_probe: `gardener@garden: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 2; line whole true, bond @ tight; spoken gardener, perspective, garden; pivots 7 (5 read)`
 four_exists: "What already comes in fours: the four walls (c:js/modes/spw/line-joints.ts:18; c:js/modes/spw/line-edit.ts:25-30; w:packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pivots.ts:50; q:pivot.js:91); in the canvas joints, four doing marks, four walls, four seams and four bonds (line-joints.ts:17-18, :27-28); four frame directions answered in six contexts (frame-context.ts:13-21); and the tool window, which opens toward the centre from whichever quarter of the screen its handle is in and turns when carried a tenth past the middle (c:js/ui/tool-window.ts:38-43, :84, :92-105). That window is the only true two-by-two split of the screen in the source."
 not_four: "What looks like four and is not: the stage has nine marks, three by three (stage-mark.ts:18-24); the node ring has eight seats and a body flick eight sectors (c:js/simulation/nodes/verb-ring.ts:20-31; body-gestures.ts:227-253); strata are three, a tool's levels three, the scale planes five. The long-press ring seats the four walls with a fifth, the loose node, at minus 90, minus 45, 45, 90 and 135 degrees (c:js/simulation/events.ts:41-47): walls next to each other on it sit 135, 45, 45 and 135 degrees apart, so a turn to the next wall is never a quarter turn."
 four_seating: "The four walls sit around a circle in two different ways. Seating one is concept, scene, mode, body, round again. The workbench pivot reader turns round it (pivots.ts:50, :314-316) and the long-press ring seats it, read clockwise (events.ts:41-47). The canvas joints, spw.quest's guide order and the order its first steps teach the four ways to hold list the walls in that order without turning round it (line-joints.ts:18, :157-161; q:pivot.js:88; q:steps.js:41), and the canvas line field lists it backward (line-edit.ts:25-30). Seating two is mode, body, scene, concept: a tap turns round it on spw.quest (q:pivot.js:91, :141-143), and the canvas node ring turns body, scene, concept the same way (c:js/simulation/nodes/line-verbs.ts:39, :52-63)."
 four_seating_cost: "In seating one, mode faces concept and scene faces body, and the two walls the babble calls the observer's (scene, mode) are neighbours. In seating two, scene faces mode. So a first turn of a body lands on a concept in the workbench's reader and on a scene on spw.quest and on the canvas node ring, and the babble's observer half and thing half exist only in seating one."
 four_quadripartite: "A quadripartite canvas maps onto the four walls and the tool window's quarters. It would have to invent a single seating, quarters of equal turn (the ring has five seats and the anatomy stacks its slots in bands top to bottom; line-anatomy.ts:70-76, :102-107), and a centre for a body written with no word, which today hangs from a dot of radius 8 (line-anatomy.ts:197)."
 turned_frame: "A frame turned 90 degrees is half built. A line written left to right is already drawn top to bottom, a concept written before the word above it and one written after below (line-anatomy.ts:1-4, :82-88), and a side rail is already scrubbed up and down (edge-scrub.ts:406-419). The top and the bottom are already taken: the title and its hash, the page's name and identity, sit at the top with the one top-edge gesture (frame-refresh.ts:701-707, :740-743); the handle, the menu whose foot says what the last press did, and the corner box with the held line sit at the bottom (focal-point.ts:450-460; c:js/ui/hotkey-buttons.ts:47; c:js/ui/held-expressions.ts:91-95). What it would have to invent is a rail along the top and one along the bottom."
}

^"art_music"{
 # Three small experiments on whether scale is useful to an artist or a musician. Each: what exists, the smallest missing piece, what a person would see or hear, and a heuristic that would settle it.
 prior: "Not repeated here: whether a sound on a brace is a reading or a decoration is the trial card wonder_trial_modality, which already records that kind and depth share one pitch dial; that the angle pair is the one pair the scan does not read is in w:.spw/caches/journal/2026-11-13-said-and-sounded.spw:88."
 hear_today: "What spw hear does, run here at cf41ca22: one click a brace, pitch by kind (392 Hz for a body, 523 for a mode, 659 for a scene), a whole tone lower each depth, a label as timbre, a close as its open backward, and one fixed gap between clicks (w:packages/spw-cli/src/hear.ts:64-71; w:packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/sound/pair-sound.ts:64-72, :220-237). Names, marks and separators make no sound."
 hear_nest: "day{wake{eat{sleep{day}}}} wrote 8 clicks in 1.6 s: 392, 349, 311, 277 Hz going in and the same coming out."
 hear_four: "door[closed]{hinge, frame, key}(threshold)<home> wrote 6 clicks for 3 pairs. Three of its four walls sound."
 hear_seam: "day{wake, eat, sleep} and day{wake; eat; sleep} each wrote 2 clicks in 0.8 s, and the two files are the same bytes. The spoken reader tells them apart, as list of 3 and sequence of 3."
 hear_gap: "With --gap 0.18 the same two clicks took 1.3 s in place of 0.8: the gap stretches silence only, and a click stays 0.045 s (pair-sound.ts:68). Two speeds of one line can be written to two files; nothing lays one over the other."
 hear_outline: "day{wake{…}} wrote 4 clicks in 1.1 s: 392, 349, 349, 392, the outer two pairs of the whole line's four. It is what the canvas's summary at depth one would give for the nested line, worked out by reading the function and not by running it."
 probe_nest: `day{wake{eat{sleep{day}}}}: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, parts 1; spoken day, definition, wake, definition, eat, definition, sleep, definition, day; end eat; end wake; end day; pivots 4 (4 read)`
 probe_four: `door[closed]{hinge, frame, key}(threshold)<home>: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, separator "," parts 3; spoken door, mode closed, definition, list of 3: hinge, frame, key; scene threshold, concept home; pivots 0`
 probe_comma: `day{wake, eat, sleep}: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, separator "," parts 3; spoken day, definition, list of 3: wake, eat, sleep; pivots 0`
 probe_semicolon: `day{wake; eat; sleep}: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, separator ";" parts 3; spoken day, definition, sequence of 3: wake, eat, sleep; pivots 0`
 probe_outline: `day{wake{…}}: parser errors 1 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, parts 1; spoken day, definition, wake, definition, unread …; end day [unread 1]; pivots 2 (2 read)`
 seam_exists: "Experiment one, hear the seam. Exists: the clicks above, and a line reader that already gives a body's parts and its separator."
 seam_missing: "Smallest missing piece: a sound for each part, placed between its pair's two clicks and timed by the separator, and a way to sound two things at one moment. Today the renderer only lays pieces end to end (pair-sound.ts:220-237)."
 seam_hears: "A person would hear the comma line as one chord between two clicks and the semicolon line as three notes in turn."
 seam_heuristic: "A musician told nothing sorts six files into together and in turn, and says which of two files had one separator changed."
 outline_exists: "Experiment two, the outline and the whole. Exists: the canvas folds a line at a depth (c:js/modes/spw/line-summary.ts:107), and the outline's four clicks against the whole's eight, as run above."
 outline_missing: "Smallest missing piece: a fold by depth in the workbench whose output reads back. The fold lives only in the canvas (no summary by depth under w:packages), and its fold glyph is one parser error and an unread word to the spoken reader."
 outline_hears: "A person would hear the outline, then the whole; with the first experiment's piece, both at once, the outline as a slower voice inside the whole."
 outline_heuristic: "Given an outline, a musician picks its whole line out of three. That would show zooming out heard as reduction, with nothing shrunk and no travel between the two."
 strata_exists: "Experiment three, three grains on one stage. Exists: every body keeps its own stratum (c:js/modes/spw/brace-folds.ts:19-30), so one line can show one body as written, a sibling by its parts and a third as particles at the same time, and a still of it can be kept (c:js/ui/hash-gestures.ts:95-103)."
 strata_missing: "Smallest missing piece: the strata travelling with the picture. They last one visit and are in neither the address nor a kept frame (brace-folds.ts:1-2; c:ts/stage/frame.ts:9-15), so a composition cannot be reopened or sent."
 strata_sees: "A person would see one line as one picture at three grains: text, figure and charge."
 strata_heuristic: "An artist composes a line at mixed strata and sends it; the receiver sees the same picture, and a second viewer can say which body is the same thing drawn finer."
 mosaic_note: "A file drawn whole is already a mosaic of lines (c:js/modes/spw/file-map.ts:83-129), and its cells cannot be moved by a hand: map regions are fixed, and a fixed region takes no drag (file-map.ts:109; c:js/simulation/rects/region-rects.ts:160)."
 reading: "All three test the babble's two_scales with what exists: none needs a hand to travel between scales. Each asks whether two scales held at once read as one thing."
}

^"fluency"{
 # A measure made of numbers the source already holds or could count, then applied once.
 stops_per_goal: "Stops passed between where the hand starts and the goal, beside the fewest any gesture needs. A rail gives it directly: the stop index is the anchor plus the travel over 32 px (c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:406-419)."
 kinds_per_rail: "Kinds of stop on one strip, read from the stop ids (tree, body, thread; edge-scrub.ts:197-230)."
 gestures_per_task: "Distinct gestures a task needs. The canvas already records which gesture a visitor has found on which surface, and the last 14 acts with a time each (c:js/ui/gesture-found.ts:25-38; c:js/ui/activation-trail.ts:8-15, :25)."
 take_back: "Whether a move can be taken back, before and after. Before: a scrub brought back inside 14.4 px commits nothing (edge-scrub.ts:413-414), and a swipe brought back inside 21.6 px is taken back (c:js/ui/gestures.ts:58-62). After: 9 of 29 act shapes name an inverse and no code reads it (c:js/ui/interaction-tree.ts:15, :108-178); undo exists in the node tool, the map's cast, the selection, the text field and the held-line history, each its own."
 said_is_done: "The share of notes whose act happened. Two cases at 1a4157a fall short by reading: a scrubbed control or swatch (facet found, said_not_done) and the fold word on a slow pinch (facet found, cue_not_act)."
 px_under_finger: "How far the thing under the finger moves because of the press itself. The site consumer's cache has the first numbers: the more row moves the rows under the finger 13 to 17 px, and the save button widens 24 px."
 hand_and_view: "How evenly steps of the hand become steps of the view: the ratio between the largest and the smallest change one equal step makes. A rail of one kind scores one; the body stops score up to 1.57 by the refit (facet zoom, refit)."
 reads_back: "The share of what a surface says that reads back as Spw. Prior art: s:workbench-report.spw host_orders_and_sides measured the breadcrumb. Counts only, probed here in the forms the canvas writes at 1a4157a, with example counts and titles filled into its templates: 4 scale notes, 4 rail stops, 3 step lines, and 8 menu receipts and verb stops with their count and title (c:js/ui/interaction-tree.ts:112-114, :181-184; c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:554). Of those 19, one reads whole in the line reader and clean in the parser: !refresh."
 reads_back_stems: "The receipts' stems, before the count and the title are joined on, do read: 5 of 6 in both readers (.-node is one parser error). What breaks a string is what joins its parts: a middle dot, an arrow, a chevron, a times sign, and a count written ~5/9. The two short stops of d4e3979 that were probed, #select and !all, both read."
 probe_receipt_emitted: `!prune{selection} ~5/9 · remove: parser errors 1 warnings 0 statements 4; line whole false, rest " ~5/9 · remove"; spoken action prune, definition, selection; potential 5/9, unread ·, remove [unread 1]; pivots 4 (0 read)`
 probe_scale_note: `@stage · ×1.42 → #>close: parser errors 3 warnings 0 statements 3; line whole false, rest " · ×1.42 → #>close"; spoken perspective stage, unread ·, ×1.42, unread →, anchor close [unread 2]; pivots 3 (0 read)`
 probe_step_line: `@node › #select[2/6]: parser errors 1 warnings 0 statements 2; line whole false, rest " › #select[2/6]"; spoken perspective node, unread ›, vibration select, mode 2/6 [unread 1]; pivots 3 (0 read)`
 probe_receipt_stem: `!prune{selection}: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true, parts 1; spoken action prune, definition, selection; pivots 4 (4 read)`
 probe_short_stop: `#select: parser errors 0 warnings 0 statements 1; line whole true; spoken vibration select; pivots 3 (3 read)`
 # Applied once.
 task: "The owner's scene, one step of it: a document of 12 lines is pasted, its first line is held and shows 3 body stops, menus are closed. Goal: hold line 8 with one scrub of the left rail."
 task_rail_before: "At 1a4157a the rail holds 16 stops of three kinds: the pasted file itself, which the tree lists (c:js/modes/spw/spw-talk.ts:136-143; c:js/modes/spw/spw-tree.ts:480-488), 3 bodies and 12 lines. It starts on the first stop marked current, which is the file and not the held line (edge-scrub.ts:236, :197-230)."
 task_numbers_before: "Stops to the goal: 11, which is 352 px, beside 7 by the down arrow. Kinds passed: 3. The goal is not among the 7 stops shown until the hand has gone 8 stops, 256 px (c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:512-517). A release 8 or more stops short lands on a body and refits the camera; a release where it began commits nothing."
 task_take_back: "Taken back before release by returning to the start; after it, by one swipe on the hash to the line held before (c:js/ui/hash-gestures.ts:74-85). Said is done: yes, a line stop is held directly (frame-refresh.ts:621-623)."
 task_worst: "At the cache's worst case of 34 stops, the last is 33 steps and 1,056 px from the first: more than the 844 px height of the phone the canvas's own check uses, so one scrub cannot reach it. A rail that starts on a file passes up to 9 more files and 12 bodies before the first line."
 task_after: "At d4e3979 the same rail holds lines only and starts on the held line: 7 stops, 224 px, one kind, the goal in view after 4 stops (edge-scrub.ts:247-296 at d4e3979). By this measure the branch's change is worth 4 stops, 128 px and two kinds on this task."
 task_px: "Nothing in the cache measures what moves under the finger on a rail. By the stylesheet the rail's card follows the finger and its rows sit about 22 px apart while a stop is 32 px of travel (c:stylesheets/widgets/concept-step.scss:59-62, :110-116; frame-refresh.ts:510), so a stop seen three rows away is four and a half rows of travel away. Not measured in a browser."
}

^"broken"{
 # Babble claims tried against the source. The first is the one this reading set out to break.
 gestures: "Broken as a description and weaker than stated as a rule. The claim: one gesture for each kind of change, no two gestures for one change, no gesture doing two kinds. On either host only the pull down makes one kind; pinch makes four kinds through eleven meanings; eight gestures step the thread and at least nine move the camera (facet gestures)."
 gestures_assignments: "Each of its three assignments misses what is built. Pinch as scale and spacing: a pinch also loads pages, folds, and primes a turn or a drop. A twist turns a wall by 90: nothing reads a twist, a wall turns by tap, swipe, spread, ring or drop, and on the one ring that seats the walls a turn to the next wall is 135 or 45 degrees, never 90 (facet sides, not_four). Scroll as sequence and time: a scroll pans, and there are five sequences it would have to choose among (facet gestures, scroll_is_space, five_times)."
 gestures_rule: "As a rule it leaves out the chooser. A kind of change is not one thing: sequence has five streams and at least three grains, scale has a node, a body, a title and a camera. The source's own chooser is the surface and the tempo (c:js/ui/gestures.ts:1-8; c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:1), and the trial card wonder_trial_grain already holds a grain belonging to a gesture as one of four readings. What the rows nearly obey is narrower: on one surface, at one tempo, one gesture makes one kind."
 zoom_doubt: "Weaker than stated. Document, line, body and part are one recursive kind in the source, drawn one way at every depth; the kinds that differ are the tree of files and the letters of a word, and both of those are already cuts. The remedy the babble offers is built where it applies. What is missing is the opposite: a continuous move where the nodes could stay, from a file drawn whole into one line and from a node into its own page (facet zoom)."
 evaluation_is_navigation: "Weaker on the rails as built. At both commits the right rail holds acts not yet taken and recent acts, which it runs again (c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:582-620 at 1a4157a, :604-609 at d4e3979); what came of an act is said at the menu's foot and beside the handle, on neither rail (c:js/ui/hotkey-buttons.ts:46-47; c:js/ui/handle-said.ts:10-22). Scrubbing back through what was done repeats it; it does not rewind it."
 rotated_frame: "Half right for a different reason. The frame is already turned in how a line is drawn and in where the title and the receipts sit (facet sides, turned_frame). Pull to refresh is not an instance: it reloads the page and can drop unsaved changes (frame-refresh.ts:345, :374); nothing a name yields comes down with it."
 two_scales: "Its example is weaker than stated: a line as a two-speed canon through spw hear has nothing to play, since a body of three parts is two clicks at any gap and no two voices can sound together (facet art_music, hear_seam, hear_gap). Its other half holds: the fractal summary is a reduction and not a shrinking (facet zoom, fractal_summary)."
}

^"wonders"{
 # Open, for the owner to judge. Each is said as something a stranger can or cannot do, so it can be tried.
 one_kind_a_strip: "A stranger scrubbing a rail can say what kind of thing the next stop is without reading its label. Today's count is three kinds at 1a4157a and one at d4e3979; would the same hold for a swipe, a flick and an arrow, each stepping one grain?"
 said_is_done: "A stranger can trust a note without looking at the stage. Counted as notes said over acts done on a scripted run; two shortfalls were read here and none measured."
 pinch_never_cuts: "A stranger can tell before letting go whether a motion will keep what is on the stage. Tried as: no pinch, spread or scrub ends by replacing the nodes or loading a page, and every move that does is a tap or a step."
 even_steps: "A stranger stepping between sibling bodies sees one thing hold still: the scale stays put among siblings and changes only when the depth does. Tried as the ratio of largest to smallest view change per equal step, which is up to 1.57 between siblings by the constants. Is this what the owner felt as on its way to hyperbolic, and does a rest at each stop bring the moment back?"
 the_bond_has_a_place: "A stranger holding a joined line can reach every nuance of it without first choosing a side. For =foo@(<bar>) seven of eleven pivots belong to the bond; do two halves need a middle, and is that middle what a hemispheric canvas is for?"
 one_seating: "A stranger who learns how a wall turns on spw.quest can say what the same turn gives on factshift.center without being told. Today a body's first turn is a scene on one and a concept in the workbench's reader; which circle seats the observer's walls side by side?"
 hear_the_seam: "A listener can tell a list from a sequence, and an outline from its whole, without seeing the line. Today the first pair is the same bytes."
 back_by_the_mirror: "A stranger can take back the last move with the reverse of the gesture that made it, without finding a menu. Counted as moves whose inverse is the mirrored gesture; today a scrub back along recent acts runs them again, and the inverse the canvas names for nine acts is read by nothing."
}

^"unverified"{
 not_driven: "Nothing was driven in a browser. Every canvas claim is a reading of source at 1a4157a. The swallowed click and the second gesture on one touch are corroborated only by the message of 423f520, which reports them driven on the branch and fixed, and that of d4e3979, which reports a re-check passing."
 deployed: "Whether d4e3979 is deployed was not checked; no network request was made. The seed calls 1a4157a deployed."
 not_heard: "Nothing was heard. The WAV files in navigation-scratch beside this file were written and their clicks counted from what spw hear printed; two were compared byte for byte."
 row_pitch: "The rail's row spacing of about 22 px is stylesheet arithmetic with a default line height assumed."
 refit_numbers: "The refit figures (1.70, 1.08, 1.57) are computed by width alone for a stage 390 px wide; a body's height can bind first."
 task_numbers: "The applied task assumes the pasted file is alone in its directory and the held line shows 3 body stops. That the rail starts on the file was read from the code, not seen."
 root_exposed: "How often a touch at the very edge lands on the root element, which decides whether the frame's swipe also runs at 1a4157a, depends on layout and was not measured."
 inverse_count: "9 of 29 counts the branches of the function that infers an act's shape, not the verbs of a live menu."
 cache_numbers: "The site consumer's measurements (13 to 17 px, 24 px, 700 ms, 2.4 s, 34 stops) are carried as written. Their clocks were found in source (c:js/ui/hotkey-buttons.ts:57; c:stylesheets/core/root.scss:35; c:js/simulation/pinch.ts:526; c:js/ui/stage-marks.ts:123) and the 34 as 10 plus 12 plus 12."
 disk_kernel: "The disk geometry kernel (mobius, geodesic, ring) is a proposal in the workbench journal to lift code from the story consumer (w:.spw/caches/journal/2026-11-11-one-table-many-scales.spw:64-76). No such code is in the workbench, and the story consumer's disk was not read."
 quest_read: "On spw.quest only the pivot's instrument was read in full; walk.js and steps.js were read by outline and hold no gesture of their own. Seating two there is read from q:pivot.js:141-143 and was not run."
 from_recall: "Nothing here rests on the seed's from_recall line."
}

^"sources"{
 prior_art: "Homes that already hold a neighbouring idea, cited and not repeated: the site consumer's ask host_orders_and_sides and its three siblings (s:workbench-report.spw:503-555); its caches s:caches/motion-and-marks-2026-11.spw:44-83 and s:caches/workbench-interaction-theory-2026-11.spw:95-107, :131-153 (the pivot ring, a feel harness); the workbench line kit's intake rows pivots, held_line_verbs, level_slider, contact_sheet, fold_pairs and spoken_twin, and its note that one-slot turns are built three times (w:.agents/plans/line-kit/wip.spw:51-80, :128); the trial cards wonder_trial_grain, wonder_trial_prime_actualize, wonder_trial_turn, wonder_trial_centre, wonder_trial_modality, wonder_trial_inside and wonder_trial_observer_postfix (w:.agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw:715, :290, :699, :664, :529, :921, :306); the journal's hyperbolic_nesting (w:.spw/caches/journal/2026-11-11-one-table-many-scales.spw:64-76)."
 new_here: "What this adds to those homes: the gesture table with its counts; the note that says and does not do; the two seatings of the four walls; the three mechanisms as the test for zoom or cut; the byte-identical WAV files; the bond's seven pivots; the fluency numbers and one task run through them."
 canvas_gestures: "c:js/ui/gestures.ts:1-8, :53-62; c:js/ui/focal-point.ts:364-436; c:js/ui/hash-gestures.ts:81-103; c:js/ui/held-expressions.ts:57-60, :91-95, :144-146, :180, :199-203; c:js/ui/tool-tiles.ts:9-16; c:js/simulation/events.ts:40-47, :95-101, :117-162, :183; c:js/simulation/nodes/handling/circle.ts:56, :188, :319-337, :417, :468, :645-685; c:js/simulation/nodes/verb-ring.ts:20-31, :49; c:js/simulation/nodes/line-verbs.ts:39-40, :74-94; c:js/simulation/rects/region-rects.ts:160-206; c:js/init/hotkeys/_.ts:101, :154-167, :196-232, :249-250, :278, :311, :330."
 canvas_rails: "At 1a4157a: c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:1-2, :82-94, :197-236, :243-320, :327-388, :396-419; c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:76-82, :345, :385, :438-455, :510-517, :547-651, :687-793, :850, :862-908; c:js/ui/frame-context.ts:11-21, :145-328; c:js/ui/tool-steps.ts:1-34; c:stylesheets/widgets/concept-step.scss:59-143. At d4e3979: c:js/ui/edge-scrub.ts:13-20, :238-296, :304-342, :497; c:js/ui/frame-refresh.ts:88, :527, :744, :756."
 canvas_scale: "c:js/simulation/pinch.ts:1-52, :122-161, :186-190, :267-283, :324-349, :384-464, :474-594; c:js/ui/scale-cue.ts:1-93; c:js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:1-44, :92-101, :166-175, :223-255, :284-319; c:js/modes/spw/brace-folds.ts:1-49; c:js/ui/title-layout.ts:1-19, :127-134; c:js/ui/tool-window.ts:38-43, :84-105; c:ts/simulation/stage-mark.ts:1-24; c:ts/stage/frame.ts:9-15."
